=== dlon(21)

Solving 5 * cos(x) ^ 2 - 12 * sin(x) * cos(x) = 2 for x

Tidying to 5 * cos(x) ^ 2 + -12 * sin(x) * cos(x) = 2

5 * cos(x) ^ 2 + -6 * sin(2 * x) = 2

Offending set is [cos(x), sin(2 * x)]

Reduced term is cos(x)

Rewriting equation in terms of cos(x)
gives 5 * cos(x) ^ 2 + -6 * (1 * (2 * cos(x) * (1 - cos(x) ^ 2) ^ (1 / 2))) = 2

Substituting   x9 for cos(x) gives
 -12 * x9 * (1 + -1 * x9 ^ 2) ^ (1/2) + 5 * x9 ^ 2 = 2

Trying to isolate 1 + -1 * x9 ^ 2
 in -12 * x9 * (1 + -1 * x9 ^ 2) ^ (1/2) + 5 * x9 ^ 2 = 2

Assuming -12 * x9 is non-zero

    1 + -1 * x9 ^ 2 = (1/144) * x9 ^ -2 * (2 + -5 * x9 ^ 2) ^ 2
     (by Isolation)

Polynomial 1 + -1 * x9 ^ 2 + (-1/144) * x9 ^ -2 * (2 + -5 * x9 ^ 2) ^ 2 becomes 

(-169/144) * x9 ^ 2 + (41/36) + (-1/36) * x9 ^ -2 when in normal form

Multiply through by x9 ^ 2 to get 

(-169/144) * x9 ^ 4 + (41/36) * x9 ^ 2 + (-1/36) = 0

This is a hidden polynomial in x9 ^ 2

Using quadratic equation formula

Solutions are x9 ^ 2 = (82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2) and x9 ^ 2 = (82/169) + (-72/169) * (-1 * (7/6) ^ (1/2))

    x9 = ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # x9 = -1 * ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # x9 = ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # x9 = -1 * ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)
     (by Isolation)

Applying substitution 
    x9 = cos(x)

   to    : 
    x9 = ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # x9 = -1 * ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # x9 = ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # x9 = -1 * ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)

   gives : 
    cos(x) = ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # cos(x) = -1 * ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # cos(x) = ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # cos(x) = -1 * ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)



Solving disjunct cos(x) = ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)

	Letting n25 denote an arbitrary integer
    x = arccos(((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)) + 360 * n25 # x = -1 * arccos(((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)) + 360 * n25
     (by Isolation)


Solving disjunct cos(x) = -1 * ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)

	Letting n26 denote an arbitrary integer
    x = arccos(-1 * ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)) + 360 * n26 # x = -1 * arccos(-1 * ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)) + 360 * n26
     (by Isolation)


Solving disjunct cos(x) = ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)

	Letting n27 denote an arbitrary integer
    x = arccos(((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)) + 360 * n27 # x = -1 * arccos(((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)) + 360 * n27
     (by Isolation)


Solving disjunct cos(x) = -1 * ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)

	Letting n28 denote an arbitrary integer
    x = arccos(-1 * ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)) + 360 * n28 # x = -1 * arccos(-1 * ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)) + 360 * n28
     (by Isolation)

Answer is : 
(X1 # (X2 # (X3 # (X4 # (X5 # (X6 # (X7 # X8)))))))
  where :
    X1 =  x = 360 * n25 + arccos(((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2))
    X2 =  x = 360 * n25 + -1 * arccos(((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2))
    X3 =  x = 360 * n26 + arccos(-1 * ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2))
    X4 =  x = 360 * n26 + -1 * arccos(-1 * ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2))
    X5 =  x = 360 * n27 + arccos(((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2))
    X6 =  x = 360 * n27 + -1 * arccos(((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2))
    X7 =  x = 360 * n28 + arccos(-1 * ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2))
    X8 =  x = 360 * n28 + -1 * arccos(-1 * ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2))


